 ## Reports
 
-`report_eval.py FLOW` creates `report-full.html` and `report-data.json` with every declared metric, planned/scored coverage, attempt failures, known and unknown cost, latency quantiles, synthetic labels, integrity status, per-case outputs, grader explanations and escaped traces. It is local and needs no external JS/CDN. It does not declare a winner. Scored means exclude unscored attempts and must be read alongside coverage.
+`report_eval.py FLOW` creates `report-full.html` and `report-data.json` with every declared metric, planned/scored coverage, attempt failures, known and unknown cost, latency quantiles, synthetic labels, integrity status, per-case outputs, grader explanations and escaped traces. It is local and needs no external JS/CDN. It does not declare a winner. Scored means exclude unscored attempts and must be read alongside coverage. Started attempts without a finished outcome remain counted as interrupted attempts with unknown cost; even when there are no finished calls, the report cannot label their total spend zero. Reports check required per-result measurement/treatment/case bindings as well as byte hashes, and mark mismatched ownership unverified.
 
 `build-report.mjs FLOW` retains the attributed upstream lite viewer for older workflows and trajectory files. It emphasizes the primary metric and legacy trace naming; use the full reporter for the new runner's hashed trace paths and all-metric evidence. The lite viewer is not a second decision engine.
 
